1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,100
Ah

2
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,160
Good morning, master.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:29,960
Ah! Good morning, Master.

4
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,100
Good morning, Grandmaster Rudeus.

5
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,360
How are you today?

6
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,020
Good morning, Xenobah.

7
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:36,520
I'm good, Julie.

8
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:37,780
Huh?

9
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:47,720
Hey, good morning, Boss.

10
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:49,140
You're looking bright-eyed.

11
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,640
And bushy-chilled.

12
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,800
Meow! What's the big idea?

13
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,320
No-no-no-no.

14
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,680
Guess the Boss finally went into heat.

15
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,500
I bet it's because of my charm.

16
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:05,120
I'm a simple temptress.

17
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:08,420
If you became the Boss's woman, you would never run out of meat.

18
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,880
Rudeus, what's up with you?

19
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,180
How do you mean?

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,660
I don't know.

21
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,760
You just have this look about you.

22
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:18,000
Like you're bursting with confidence.

23
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,140
If I can have your attention, I guess I have an announcement.

24
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:27,220
Although I can't reveal the details right now,

25
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,080
I was cured of a long-term ailment yesterday.

26
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,840
Dang, I had no idea you were sick, Boss.

27
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,520
Yeah, is that why you never jumped our bones or anything?

28
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:37,800
Many heartfelt congratulations.

29
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:41,160
Although you could have confided in me at any time.

30
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,480
So that's it.

31
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:43,760
You must have struggled.

32
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:45,740
Congratulations, Rudeus.

33
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:51,840
The disease that plagued my first year at the University of Magic

34
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,380
is no more.

35
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,600
All thanks to Sylphie,

36
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,860
who gave me something precious to help me through it.

37
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:03,680
I finally feel human again.

38
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:07,000
Now he smells even more in heat!

39
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,600
He's a threat to the chastity of every one of us!

40
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,020
Keep your distance or you're lined up preggers!

41
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,320
How uncouth.

42
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:15,080
I'm a gentleman, you know.

43
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:23,360
If you were to date someone, Nanohoshi,

44
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,380
what kinds of things would you want or expect from them?

45
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,340
I take it that's your idea of small talk today?

46
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:32,780
Something like that.

47
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:34,920
All you ever do is chit-chat.

48
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,060
Would you take this seriously?

49
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,820
I'd like to get home as soon as I can.

50
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:43,280
And we'll work far more efficiently if you keep quiet.

51
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,660
Okay, don't get defensive.

52
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:48,040
I take it you've never been in love then?

53
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:48,940
Tch.

54
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,560
Of course I have.

55
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,000
Although,

56
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:57,580
we had a fight and I haven't seen him since.

57
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,000
Ah, right.

58
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,780
Nanohoshi was summoned in the middle of an argument.

59
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,040
Sorry.

60
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,020
You don't need to apologize.

61
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,060
Just work.

62
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:12,080
And if I like someone,

63
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,960
just spending time together is enough.

64
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:22,360
I've been sending the occasional letter to Paul to keep him updated.

65
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:24,340
And now that I'm cured,

66
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,960
I could work to reunite with my family.

67
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,180
But there's one more thing I want to embark on first.

68
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:39,260
I want to do right by Sylphie.

69
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:41,100
She helped me.

70
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,500
Now it's my turn to provide for her as a husband.

71
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:46,240
Oh.

72
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:47,820
Actually, wait.

73
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:51,680
How do you get married in this world?

74
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,900
Marriage, Master?

75
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:57,640
Weddings.

76
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:01,080
I just realized I don't know what's considered traditional.

77
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,440
Well, let me think.

78
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:04,180
You start with the house, right?

79
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:05,120
Mm-hmm.

80
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,740
Oh, you jump straight to a house?

81
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,960
Yeah, of course you do.

82
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:12,080
How can you get married if you don't even have a place to live?

83
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,000
Fair enough.

84
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:18,420
Paul and Zenith settled down in Buena Village as soon as they married, too.

85
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:23,120
It would be one thing if you married a well-to-do girl who already had a home of her own.

86
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:27,060
But if neither of you do, the man shows his worth by getting one.

87
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,200
Okay, a little culture shock there.

88
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:31,640
Understood.

89
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,900
Then a house will come first.

90
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,620
I'll go into town tomorrow to look at some.

91
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:37,620
Wait a sec.

92
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,160
You're already engaged?

93
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:39,840
Yeah.

94
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:40,840
Kinda.

95
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:41,940
To who?

96
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:46,140
To, uh, the person who cured my illness.

97
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:47,540
Keep your secrets, then.

98
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,800
But if she's a follower of Mealus, do let me know, okay?

99
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:54,800
I can't conduct a full service yet, but I can give a blessing.

100
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:55,760
Thanks.

101
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,700
I came in here without a plan.

102
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:09,740
I honestly have no idea how nice a place I should try to aim for.

103
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:14,680
Sylvie guards a princess, and work aside, they're good friends.

104
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:18,280
Which means Princess Ariel might come to visit from time to time.

105
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:23,060
So I guess we'll need a pretty nice place, then, won't we?

106
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:28,040
Maybe I should have brought Sylvie to get her input on all this.

107
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:29,720
No, no.

108
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,940
I've got to show her she can count on me.

109
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:35,300
A big house with plenty of rooms.

110
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,360
That doesn't cost too much.

111
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,580
Oh?

112
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:38,620
Oh.

113
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,020
What a lovely place.

114
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:57,160
It's a little big for two people, isn't it?

115
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,000
Maybe.

116
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,460
But its reputation drove down the price.

117
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,740
You said the housing authority thinks that it's cursed?

118
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:10,420
There are reports of a scraping sound in the middle of the night, and apparently its previous residents were murdered inside.

119
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,880
Did they try an exorcism?

120
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:18,340
The first party to do it was mangled, too, so the Adventurer's Guild took the job down.

121
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,600
The Mages Guild won't touch it either.

122
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,320
Talk about negligent.

123
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,640
That's why I called you two in.

124
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:30,760
Now then, on your guards, gentlemen, and let's get to it!

125
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:38,800
Huh.

126
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:42,040
Hey, what's your problem? Don't just start breaking things!

127
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:45,700
Pardon me. The door was warped and wouldn't open otherwise.

128
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,280
Huh.

129
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,040
Master, how shall we proceed?

130
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:57,300
We'll start on the ground floor here. Sweep the rooms counterclockwise.

131
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,860
Understood, Master.

132
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:02,000
Huh. You're being awfully official about this.

133
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,520
I am an A-ranked adventurer, and I'm gonna live here, so...

134
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:07,760
Alright. Yeah, I guess you are.

135
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,720
In that case, what do you want me to do?

136
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:15,120
If we do run into anything, I'd like you to attack with elementary divine magic.

137
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,720
Okay, I can do that.

138
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:26,460
When you come to, it's crazy.

139
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,220
Another try, God, I need you to do it.

140
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:30,860
Okay.

141
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,940
Hey, God.

142
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:33,220
Hey, God.

143
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:34,100
Hi.

144
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:55,240
No signs of life.

145
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,560
But you wanted us to stay the night here, didn't you?

146
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:00,860
Yes. If that's still okay.

147
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,860
It'll be dark in here before too long.

148
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,820
Whatever's killing people is supposed to show up at night.

149
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:11,120
I'm guessing some kind of monster has made its lair here.

150
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:16,060
It shouldn't be that strong. High-ranked monsters won't come into town.

151
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:18,100
But you can't be too careful.

152
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,740
I'm a little worried about Julie.

153
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:23,100
Yeah, I've been worrying about Lise too.

154
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:26,680
I'm worried about Sylphie myself.

155
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:28,760
Sanopa.

156
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:30,420
Yes, Master?

157
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:35,600
You know, as soon as we finish this job, I'm getting married.

158
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:42,700
Yes. Let's sort this out quickly and throw a magnificent party to celebrate your matrimony.

159
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:43,920
Sounds like fun.

160
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:46,280
So you had better invite Lise and me.

161
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:51,320
Yeah, of course I will.

162
00:08:51,320 --> 00:09:03,000
Oh, my God.

163
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,880
Oh.

164
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,880
Oh!

165
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:38,880
Rudeus, wake up!

166
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,880
I hear something!

167
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:44,880
Wake Sanobab for me.

168
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,880
Huh?

169
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:54,880
Wake Sanobab for me.

170
00:09:54,880 --> 00:10:16,880
How's it look out there?

171
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,880
I can't see anything in the dark.

172
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,880
Let's sweep the house again.

173
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:22,880
Understood.

174
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:28,880
I want to put eyes on every nook and cranny,

175
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,880
so keep your wits about you.

176
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,880
Right.

177
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,880
Now all that's left is the basement.

178
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,880
Yeah.

179
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,880
What's the word?

180
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,880
No sign of anything.

181
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,880
Nothing.

182
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,880
Hmm.

183
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:06,880
Let's go back to the bedroom.

184
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,880
We can better prepare for an attack in there.

185
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,880
There's definitely something here.

186
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,880
Maybe it'll come to us.

187
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:16,880
Or maybe it'll wait until we're fast asleep again.

188
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:20,880
Now it could be lurking in here.

189
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,880
Stay on your guard.

190
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:28,880
Looks like the coast is clear, Master.

191
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,880
Hmm.

192
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:32,880
Yep, it's definitely gonna wait till we're asleep.

193
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,880
Fun exciting.

194
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,880
Huh?

195
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:46,880
Let's...

196
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:47,500
Let's find the

197
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,880
fire.

198
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,880
Annemerer.

199
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,880
Hmm?

200
00:11:55,880 --> 00:12:19,320
Begone, you!

201
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:33,940
I'm a blessed child, you recall.

202
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,100
This won't even leave a scratch.

203
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:39,380
I call upon thee, God who blesses the land, our mother with bounty!

204
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:42,560
Visit divinity upon the foolish who defies the natural ways!

205
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,560
Exorcism!

206
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,560
I'll be.

207
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:49,200
That didn't do anything!

208
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:55,640
Get out of the way!

209
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,640
Zanobar!

210
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,640
Move!

211
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,640
Please wait, master!

212
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,640
No, that's enough!

213
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,640
I'll handle it!

214
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:01,640
No, master!

215
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:02,640
Wait!

216
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:05,640
I beg of you!

217
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:18,640
Thank you.

218
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,640
Now, back to the room.

219
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:23,640
Uh, yeah.

220
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,640
What?

221
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:28,640
I wasn't running away, okay?

222
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:31,640
The hallway was so narrow, I thought I'd be in the way.

223
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:32,640
That's true.

224
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:33,640
Good call.

225
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,640
I know.

226
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,640
I'm not gonna tease you.

227
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,640
Spooked me too, man.

228
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,640
I know.

229
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,640
I know.

230
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:41,640
I know.

231
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,640
I know.

232
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,640
You're not an immortal demon king or anything.

233
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,640
Just look at it, master.

234
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,640
Oh.

235
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:50,640
Is that... a doll?

236
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:51,640
Indeed.

237
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:53,640
And a magnificent one at that.

238
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:54,640
Okay.

239
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:57,640
I know you like dolls and everything, but come on.

240
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,640
I will not.

241
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:01,640
This doll was moving of its own accord.

242
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,640
A moving doll!

243
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:04,640
Yeah.

244
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:06,640
I guess it was.

245
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,640
How about that?

246
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:11,640
Robots, automata, and mecha maids.

247
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:12,640
Oh my.

248
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,640
That really is incredible!

249
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:17,640
I'm so glad you finally understand, master.

250
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,640
Well done, Xenobah.

251
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,640
Your keen eye for dolls has already surpassed mine.

252
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,640
Ah.

253
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:25,640
I recognized it as a doll the moment I laid eyes on it.

254
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:28,640
A magic moving doll, huh?

255
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:32,640
If we can figure out how it works, maybe we can make our own.

256
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:37,640
This one is wooden, but if we could animate a... silicone or something...

257
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,640
The possibilities...

258
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:42,640
What an amazing...

259
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:43,640
I find!

260
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,640
My heart is pounding out of my chest!

261
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,640
Oh yes.

262
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,640
Mine too.

263
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:49,640
I feel as though I may even weep.

264
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,640
What is wrong with you freaks?

265
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,640
Huh?

266
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,640
We've got more important things to worry about than a doll.

267
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:57,640
What could be more important than that?!

268
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,640
It moved entirely on its own!

269
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:02,640
Can you not see a grand significance?

270
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:04,640
I can just say you could still be a monster!

271
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,640
Xenobah, you can let go of him now.

272
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:09,640
But master...

273
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:12,640
Sorry, but Master Cliff has a point.

274
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,640
I mean...

275
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:15,640
The doll probably is our evil spirit.

276
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,640
Oh.

277
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:18,640
And it might not be alone.

278
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:20,640
We need to find that out.

279
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:24,640
And if we're lucky, we may find schematics for making them too.

280
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,640
Oh, yes! I see your point now!

281
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:29,640
Come on, let's figure out where that thing was hiding.

282
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:30,640
Huh.

283
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,640
There's an odd scrape on the floor here.

284
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,640
I wonder if the wall is actually...

285
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:44,640
Xenobah, will you give it a push?

286
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,640
With pleasure.

287
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,640
Pleasure.

288
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:47,640
Hm.

289
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:53,640
I knew it. A hidden door.

290
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:04,640
Cliff, come here a sec. Do you know what this pedestal is for?

291
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:06,640
I don't. Totally foreign to me.

292
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:09,640
What'd you find?

293
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,640
Uh...

294
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:12,640
Book?

295
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:15,640
And it seems to have something about the doll in it.

296
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,640
Looks like there might be magic circles somewhere on the body.

297
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:21,640
How can you tell that?

298
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,640
Uh...

299
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,640
I've been studying magical implements lately.

300
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,640
I've seen a lot of similar diagrams.

301
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,640
That's fascinating.

302
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:32,640
Whoever this room belonged to either made the doll or was studying it.

303
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:36,640
Seems like it was programmed in some way to protect the house.

304
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,640
At least, that would explain all our unlucky murder victims anyway.

305
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:43,640
And with all this stuff untouched and gathering dust,

306
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:46,640
I assume the owner must have been able to do this.

307
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:47,640
It seems to be a good idea.

308
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,640
And with all this stuff untouched and gathering dust,

309
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,640
I assume the owner must have died suddenly.

310
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,640
In any case,

311
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,640
Looks like that was the only doll in the house.

312
00:16:58,640 --> 00:16:59,640
Yes.

313
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,640
In other words,

314
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,640
Case closed.

315
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:08,640
Thank you.

316
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,640
Seriously.

317
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,640
I don't know what I would have done if it wasn't for you two.

318
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,640
Don't mention it.

319
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,640
We're not strangers.

320
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,640
But, um, what are you gonna do with all that stuff?

321
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,640
I'm not sure.

322
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,640
I guess I'll borrow a spare lab to study it and...

323
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,640
Master?

324
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:27,640
Yeah? What's up?

325
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,640
Might I convince you to leave the research of this moving doll entirely to me?

326
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,640
You want to take points on all of it?

327
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,640
My monopool is beyond abysmal.

328
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,640
And my hands are clumsy.

329
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:42,640
Take for instance the red dragon figurine we're making for Julie.

330
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,640
All I have accomplished is being in the way.

331
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,640
I make the work drag on forever.

332
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:52,640
Deciphering the handwriting in the journal will probably take me some time.

333
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:56,640
The research would undoubtedly proceed faster in your hands alone, Master.

334
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,640
And yet...

335
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:02,640
What if the doll decides to go berserk again while you're studying it?

336
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:04,640
I can handle roughhousing.

337
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,640
I'm no stranger to it.

338
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,640
Well, obviously, but...

339
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:11,640
Master, I beg you.

340
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:13,640
Hear me.

341
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:14,640
When your plans finally bear fruit,

342
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,640
I want to have contributed more than just money.

343
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,640
I swear I will prove myself useful to you.

344
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,640
Please, Master. Please entrust this research to me!

345
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:29,640
Very well.

346
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:32,640
Xanoba, the doll's all yours.

347
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,640
You truly mean it?

348
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:38,640
I will say, someone kept this secret for a reason, so be careful.

349
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,640
I cannot thank you enough!

350
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:42,640
Well, keep it under control, whatever you do.

351
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,640
We don't need that thing rampaging.

352
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:46,640
Least of all at school.

353
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:52,640
I made an unexpected find, and I've got the home of my dreams.

354
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,640
My, whatever do you want to show me out here, Rudy?

355
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,640
I simply can't wait to find out.

356
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,640
Your delivery is so wooden, Sylphie.

357
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:09,640
I wonder, could it be that you did some snooping around and already know what your surprise is?

358
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,640
Why?

359
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:14,640
What do you mean?

360
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,640
I don't know what you're talking about.

361
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:43,640
I had the contractors get something close to your original hair color for the roof.

362
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,640
I always really liked your hair.

363
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,640
Even if you didn't.

364
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:49,640
Huh?

365
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,640
Oh gosh, you're right!

366
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,640
What do you say?

367
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,640
Wanna come inside and see the rest?

368
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,640
Wanna come inside and see the rest?

369
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,640
Oh, my god.

370
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,640
Oh, my god.

371
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,640
Oh, my god.

372
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,640
Our bedroom.

373
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,640
It's the only room done on this floor so far.

374
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,640
Goodness.

375
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:44,640
Why do we need such a huge bed?

376
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,640
You really have to ask?

377
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:50,640
So I can savor every bite of you, of course!

378
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,640
Oh, that makes sense.

379
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:54,640
I almost forgot.

380
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,640
Uh, Sylphie.

381
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,640
Oh, yes?

382
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,640
I promised to marry you, but are we rushing into it?

383
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,640
Like, what comes next?

384
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:16,640
I bought this house for us to start, but beside that, we still have so much to talk over.

385
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:21,640
Oh, well, however many kids you want is fine with me.

386
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:23,640
Okay.

387
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:29,640
I'm definitely happy to hear it, but what about guarding Princess Ariel?

388
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:33,640
We've still got another two years in this country at least.

389
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:37,640
And we aren't planning to rush back to Asura the second we graduate.

390
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:40,640
So, um…

391
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:42,640
Sorry.

392
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,640
That's not very fair.

393
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:46,640
You deserve someone who can settle down.

394
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,640
You've provided such a beautiful home.

395
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,640
But am I really good enough?

396
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:55,640
Sylphie helped give me back a part of myself.

397
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,640
And she used her body to do it.

398
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:02,640
It was her very first time, and I was rough.

399
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:04,640
But if she was afraid…

400
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:08,640
She never showed any sign of it that I could see.

401
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:11,640
And she smiled at me in the morning.

402
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:15,640
That's what finally made me feel whole again.

403
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:20,640
So if she isn't good enough, no one is.

404
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:23,640
I have no right to be your wife, do I?

405
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:26,640
Sylphie, you're mine no matter what!

406
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:28,640
Oh, yes, yes!

407
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,640
Of course!

408
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,640
I'm yours, Rudy!

409
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:41,640
So, please, will you marry me?

410
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:43,640
Ah!

411
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,640
Yes!

412
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,640
I got the house.

413
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:56,640
You do whatever you want or need to.

414
00:22:57,640 --> 00:23:00,640
And if any issues do come up, we can talk through them.

415
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:02,640
That sounds good.

416
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:06,640
On that note, is there anything you want to tell me?

417
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:13,640
Just don't up and disappear on me, okay?

418
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,640
Okay.

419
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,640
I understand.

420
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,640
I won't disappear on you.

421
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,640
I love you.

422
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:25,640
Good.

423
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:26,640
Love you.

424
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,640
Love you.

425
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:38,640
Love you.

426
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:39,640
Love you.

427
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,640
Love you.

